Responsive results good:
- Landscape 844x390: board stage 824x259 but board rendered square size limited by height (259-2*~16=227), so board only 227px wide centered in 824. That's small, with huge empty side areas, while side panel bottom. In landscape, could improve layout by placing control panel side-by-side again (desktop-like) or board bigger? Board limited by height anyway, but stage could be narrower and panel on right, board still 227. Yet current board is tiny on landscape; perhaps the control panel should be a right sidebar in landscape to give board height? Board height limited by topbar+panel; still 259 stage; board ~228. If panel were side, board stage height 390-51-10=329 -> board ~297. Slight better. But landscape phone not primary? Agent instructions require mobile/tablet support. It is playable (board 227, cell 28px, pieces readable but touch targets 28px maybe too small). We should improve landscape by making control panel compact overlay/side. At min-width 600 and orientation landscape and max-height 570, layout should use two columns like desktop: board stage + control panel side, maybe control panel width 240. Then board square 300ish. Let's redesign landscape media query.

Currently max-height 570 landscape: `.control-panel` stays grid with 2 columns, actions row, selected hidden, panel 60 tall. Board stage 824x259. We can instead use grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) 230px and rows 1fr in landscape; control panel flex column/compact with only actions stacked? Need include fire/rotate and maybe turn card? Header already shows turn. We can make panel width 200 with actions stacked vertical; board stage width 844-20-200-10=614, height 390-51-10=329 => board size min(614-32=582,329-32=297)=297. Much better (cell 37px), still small but better. Panel height 329; actions buttons 100x? stacked, plenty. Could include rotate/fire and maybe legend hidden; selected info hidden. That leaves blank panel. We can show turn name too maybe. But minimal.

Alternatively put panel horizontally at bottom but reduce header to 0? Board height limited by panel 60; could make the control panel a floating overlay over board bottom? Then board 333 (height) width limited 844, cell 41. Better. But overlay could cover rows. Side panel better.

For orientation landscape tablets 1024x768, max-height 570 doesn't apply, and max-width 880? width 1024 >880 so desktop layout side panel; board height 690 -> good. Fine.

So add media query:
```
@media (max-height: 570px) and (orientation: landscape) {
 .game-shell { grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) 210px; grid-template-rows: minmax(0,1fr); }
 .control-panel { display:flex; flex-direction:column; padding:10px; overflow:hidden; }
 .selected-info{display:none}
 .actions { display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:8px; }
 .rotate-btn,.fire-btn { min-height:54px; width:100%; }
 .turn-card { display:block? } 
 .legend,.panel-foot {display:none}
 .action-hint,.fire-sub{display:block} maybe.
}
```
But current max-height media sets `.control-panel { grid-template-columns... }` and `.selected-info{display:none}` and actions etc. Need override properly with higher specificity or adjust the same query. The existing query comes after max-width 720/880? Order: @media max-width 880, max-width720, max-width390, then max-height landscape. So the landscape query is last. We can rewrite it fully.

At 844x390, header height 46, game shell padding 5 top bottom? `.game-shell` has padding 8 top? In max-height query `.game-shell{padding-top:5px}`. Grid columns currently from max-width 880: one column rows minmax(0,1fr) auto. Override `grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1fr) 210px; grid-template-rows:minmax(0,1fr);`. Also bottom padding from base `calc(10px + env)` remains; fine. Height available = 390-46-5-10=329.

Panel width 210. Fire button 54, rotate 54, selected info hidden, turn card hidden. If we show turn card, adds 100 height but panel has 329; could fit. Actually useful to display turn in panel? Header shows. But panel blank otherwise. Could show turn-name compact at top:
```
.turn-card { display:block; padding:10px; }
.turn-name { font-size:22px }
.turn-sub,.turn-bar {display:none}
```
Then actions at bottom via margin-top:auto. Could look intentional. Also show a small keyboard hint. But panel is 210 wide. Header turn pill enough; maybe show "TACTICAL CONSOLE" label + selected info? Keep minimal.

Fire button has vertical gradient and red; rotate above. It will be big; nice. Board largest.

But on landscape 640x360 (small phone), board stage width 640-20-? panel 200 = 410; height ~290; board 290. Fine. At 568x320 maybe panel 180. Use `clamp(180px, 26vw, 230px)`.

Need ensure header menu labels show? At max-width 720 labels hidden; landscape 844 width >720 so labels show, good. At 640 width labels hidden; header width 640 enough.

Add CSS.

Also board size in landscape with stage wider than tall: margin based height, board square 297; centered horizontally leaving side gaps. Stage could be sized to square? Board visually centered; okay. Could reduce stage width to board+small? The grid gives stage full leftover; board centered. Fine, starfield fills.

Let's implement overrides.

